From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 08:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: end the Critical Update flag at the DTIM Beacon

Depends on 602-ap-mld-announce-the-removal-of-an-affiliated-ap.patch and
on the mac80211 patches that add NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_BEACON_CRIT_UPDATE,
NL80211_ATTR_CRIT_UPDATE_ID and NL80211_CMD_CRIT_UPDATE_DONE.

IEEE 802.11be-2024 35.3.10 sets the Critical Update flag until and
including the next DTIM Beacon on the link. hostapd does not see the
DTIM Count of its Beacon frames, so patch 602 sets the flag for DTIM
period + 1 counts of the AP Removal Timer. That holds the DTIM Beacon in
every phase, but keeps the flag after it.

Where the driver declares NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_BEACON_CRIT_UPDATE, set
the flag on each link of the AP MLD when a link removal starts, and keep
it until NL80211_CMD_CRIT_UPDATE_DONE reports the DTIM Beacon of that
link. Then update the Beacon and Probe Response frames of the link
without it. Without the feature, and for a nontransmitted BSSID, which
has no Beacon frames of its own, the count of patch 602 stays.

Each critical update of a link gets a new ID, which hostapd passes with
each Beacon update that sets the flag. The driver starts a new critical
update for a new ID, also after the DTIM Beacon of the previous one, and
continues the current one for the same ID. So the updates of the AP
Removal Timer at each count do not extend the flag. The event names the
ID of the critical update that ended, so an event of an earlier critical
update does not end a later one.

Add NL80211_ATTR_STA_DUMP_LINK_STATS to nl80211_copy.h as well, so that
the attribute numbers match the kernel headers of mac80211 patch 004.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
